      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{y}^{2},\\, & \\text{if}\\,-1<x<1,\\,0<y<2, \\\\ {2}^{xy},\\, & \\text{if}\\,1<x<3,\\,0<y<2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{(-1,3)\\times (0,2)}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that the rectangle $R$ can be represented as a union of two smaller rectangles, as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =((-1,1)\\cup (1,3))\\times (0,2) \\\\  & =((-1,1)\\times (0,2))\\cup ((1,3)\\times (0,2)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{(-1,1)\\times (0,2)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(1,3)\\times (0,2)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{(-1,1)\\times (0,2)}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A\\text{ }+{∬}_{(1,3)\\times (0,2)}{2}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
